A directory can contain subfolders, which contain other subfolders, which contain files.

The -R flag commands Linux to crawl to the deepest subfolder, delete the innermost files first, work its way up deleting parent folders, and finally delete mydirectory itself:

Plaintext
mydirectory/
  ├── subfolder/
  │     └── deep_file.txt  <-- 1. Deletes this first
  └── file1.txt            <-- 2. Deletes this
                           <-- 3. Deletes empty subfolder/
                           <-- 4. Deletes empty mydirectory/
